{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1086250-essence-and-other-fuels","id":1086250,"title":"Essence and other fuels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-01T10:32:45-07:00","id":1086250,"title":"Essence and other fuels","content":"Demon's core book actually goes into what essence is and its basic function in the universe.<br /> <br /> Spirits, Claimed, Hosts, Goetics, Angels, the God Machine, Ghosts, Chthonians, some Horrors, Werewolves, and in a weird way even Mages use essence.<br /> <br /> It underlies physics to the point where its really just a misunderstood element of physics, including process of life.<br /> <br /> Using demon as a starting point I theorize that most, but not all other fuels are by products of essence.<br /> <br /> Aether that demons is the by product of the type of essence used by the God Machine.<br /> <br /> Plasm that Sin Eaters use is a by product of spent ghost essence.<br /> <br /> Sekhem is spent life essence, essence used up in natural processes.<br /> <br /> Vitae is Sekhem, and occasionally other eneegies, converted into something compatible with creatures descended from or born in the Dark Place that the Strix come from, like Kindred, Strix, Void Creatures, Ghouls, Cruac Gods, and so on.<br /> <br /> Glamour I'm not sure about, maybe the byproduct of mind essence.<br /> <br /> Mana is the symbollic supernal form of essence.<br /> <br /> Pyros/Flux proto essence, it hasn't been refined enough to become essence.<br /> <br /> Satiety I'm not sure, Satiety seems to be more how you feed, not an energy source in of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 05-01-2017, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T10:42:56-07:00","id":1086252,"title":"","content":"Satiety to me seems more like a simplification and representation of Essence. The Horror doesn't have an explicit Essence pool, but the way it feeds is similar to how spirits can gorge themselves on the correct Resonant Conditions, and Satiety can be seen as a representation of how your Beast experiences their Horror's pool. It makes sense since the Horror is basically a goetic entity and other goetia uses Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T10:48:54-07:00","id":1086254,"title":"","content":"Btw, do you have any sources that support your theories on Vitae and Sekhem? I'd like to read more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T11:16:52-07:00","id":1086265,"title":"","content":"Vitae is generally considered to be life, distilled. That's why it's so addictive, why it can move and do things on its own. It's explained this way, 'Vitae is life. Life tastes very, very good. In fact, it tastes so good, it\u2019s highly addictive to both mortal and Kindred alike.' And of course there's a big clue in the name. Vitae comes from vital which comes from the Latin vita, for life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T12:27:38-07:00","id":1086286,"title":"","content":"I get that, but is there any connection to Sekhem other than it also being described as a force of life? I get why one could make the connection, but from what I've gathered (haven't read that much MtC) they function quite differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T12:52:17-07:00","id":1086295,"title":"","content":"Sekhem is a bit more complicated than Vitae, since it can be described as the essential resonance of all life and its memories, with everything that implies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T13:43:21-07:00","id":1086315,"title":"","content":"That sounds like it is time for Supernatural Thermodynamics!<br /> <br /> *puts the chemist hat*<br /> <br /> we can all agree that the different &quot;fuels&quot; each of the supernatural breeds use is, in fact, carriers energy- which means the regular scientific rules we usually use for Work and energy should still be valid. You know, the big three rules of Thermodynamics and such things (law of energy conservation, entropy increasement, etc). We also know that the different fuels could be quantified and measured (even if the player characters can't), so we could theoretically measure how much energy is found in each unit of &quot;fuel&quot; (meaning, the joule worth of Vitae, for example). Even more interesting fact is that, like in classical thermodynamics, it looks like each of the different carriers of energy have their own conjugated variable, which defines how much energy is found on average in each amount of energy- that is, Supernatural Tolerance.<br /> <br /> If all of the fuels are simply different ways energy express itself through different dimensions (like mass, volume, amount, etc), then the way the different &quot;fuels&quot; vary from splat to splat is because each splay can utilize energy from different dimensions in order to perform work. Vitae, for example, is a standard unit of measurement which quantifies &quot;Life Force&quot;. Blood Potency is its conjugated variable (or Shadow Potency, in case of strixs), and it actually means how much of energy the vampire can gain from one unit of Life Force (joule/vitae). Essence represent the expression of object in reality (ephemerals use it in order to reinforce their existence, after all), and could be described through Rank (or Primal Urge for werewolves).<br /> <br /> Because of that, it is not that all the other fuels in the world are Essence, it is simply that by the law of energy conservation energy can not be destroyed, only transmuted from one dimension to another- and that in the environment there much much more Essence available than any other form of fuel, apparently because its energy potential (its &quot;Rank&quot;) is much lower when compared to other fuels, so investing energy in that dimension is much more profitable to the universe, energetically speaking. When you describe Aether and Plasm as being &quot;byproduct&quot; of using Essence, you actually describe how energy converts from one dimension to another, turning from the more general quantification of &quot;existence&quot; into a different dimension, just like that when you split an atom energy is converted from mass into light, volume and entropy, creating an explosion.<br /> <br /> In sort, the way I see it, it is not that all fuels are Essence- it is that all fuels are energy, and that for certain reasons, Essence is the most available carrier of energy for supernatural beings, and as such most of them adapted to utilize that resource.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T13:59:38-07:00","id":1086326,"title":"","content":"On that last bit, then why would anyone adapt to using non-Essence fuels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T14:05:26-07:00","id":1086328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1086250-essence-and-other-fuels?p=1086286#post1086286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that, but is there any connection to Sekhem other than it also being described as a force of life? I get why one could make the connection, but from what I've gathered (haven't read that much MtC) they function quite differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I should have quoted, I was responding to Omegaphallic. I don't know much about Sekhem, but if it is 'spent' life, it wouldn't fit as Vitae, as Vitae is so full of life it lets corpses and shadows come 'alive.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-01-2017, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T14:23:51-07:00","id":1086332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1086250-essence-and-other-fuels?p=1086326#post1086326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that last bit, then why would anyone adapt to using non-Essence fuels?</div> </div> </div> </div>If going with LostLight's text it'd probably be because only ephemerals (and the half-ephemeral werewolves who were created to deal with a certain type of ephemeral) have an easy time taking in energy in the form of Essence. Vampires, for example, might lack the metaphysical components that are required to handle Essence. For them it could've been easier to adapt to use Vitae for their supernatural needs.<br /> Also note that many major splats are manufactured or otherwise come to be in ways that are independent of evolution. Mummies, for example, couldn't adapt to use Essence instead of Pillars/Sekhem since their current existence is the result of the Rite of Return instead of evolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T14:28:40-07:00","id":1086335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1086250-essence-and-other-fuels?p=1086326#post1086326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that last bit, then why would anyone adapt to using non-Essence fuels?</div> </div> </div> </div>the sort answer- evolution. you don't &quot;choose&quot; which fuel you are using- you work with what you can. For example, vampires never chose drinking blood for energy- it is just how their system works. Mages Awaken with the ability to convert Mana to energy. Nobody asked them if they are ok with it- this is just how things works. Maybe long long long time ago, all supernatural beings were only able to use Essence. Then, one day, something went wrong, and instead of Essence a certain spirit discovered it can only feed upon Vitae- becoming the first of what is known is &quot;strix&quot;. Maybe another mutated spirit had the ability to use Plasm, creating a geist. Maybe the first Mages were awakened when spirits which were created with Mana affinity Claimed them in order to find a way to survive in the harsh world. Evolution doesn't ask &quot;what would you like to do&quot;. It looks on the situation, sees a mistake and says &quot;well, shit- what do we do now?&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT- what Tessie has said.","signature