know that the different fuels could be quantified and measured (even if the player characters can't), so we could theoretically measure how much energy is found in each unit of &quot;fuel&quot; (meaning, the joule worth of Vitae, for example). Even more interesting fact is that, like in classical thermodynamics, it looks like each of the different carriers of energy have their own conjugated variable, which defines how much energy is found on average in each amount of energy- that is, Supernatural Tolerance.<br /> <br /> If all of the fuels are simply different ways energy express itself through different dimensions (like mass, volume, amount, etc), then the way the different &quot;fuels&quot; vary from splat to splat is because each splay can utilize energy from different dimensions in order to perform work. Vitae, for example, is a standard unit of measurement which quantifies &quot;Life Force&quot;. Blood Potency is its conjugated variable (or Shadow Potency, in case of strixs), and it actually means how much of energy the vampire can gain from one unit of Life Force (joule/vitae). Essence represent the expression of object in reality (ephemerals use it in order to reinforce their existence, after all), and could be described through Rank (or Primal Urge for werewolves).<br /> <br /> Because of that, it is not that all the other fuels in the world are Essence, it is simply that by the law of energy conservation energy can not be destroyed, only transmuted from one dimension to another- and that in the environment there much much more Essence available than any other form of fuel, apparently because its energy potential (its &quot;Rank&quot;) is much lower when compared to other fuels, so investing energy in that dimension is much more profitable to the universe, energetically speaking. When you describe Aether and Plasm as being &quot;byproduct&quot; of using Essence, you actually describe how energy converts from one dimension to another, turning from the more general quantification of &quot;existence&quot; into a different dimension, just like that when you split an atom energy is converted from mass into light, volume and entropy, creating an explosion.<br /> <br /> In sort, the way I see it, it is not that all fuels are Essence- it is that all fuels are energy, and that for certain reasons, Essence is the most available carrier of energy for supernatural beings, and as such most of them adapted to utilize that resource.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is <i>so fucking cool.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T18:44:45-07:00","id":1086413,"title":"","content":"Oh! I got one! We can calculate the energy in a point of Mana! Assuming an improvised casting of Ex Nihilo as a Common Arcanum-spell, creating a solid block of osmium at Size 9. That puts it at bigger a compact car (100 cubic feet according to the EPA, Size 8), so we'll go with 125 cubic feet. That's about 80,000 kg. E = mc<sup>2</sup>, so that's over 7000 EXAJOULES.<br /> <br /> If we're willing to accept that &quot;Ex Nihilo&quot; lives up to its namesake, then that means that a Master of Matter, with a lot of effort (or a single Reach), can create matter with an equivalent energy to almost 30,000 times the yield of the Tsar Bomba (a pitiful 100 petajoules).<br /> <br /> Don't play with Mana, Mana is not a toy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T03:51:29-07:00","id":1086539,"title":"","content":"But Mana doesn't fuel spells, really. They can be used to fuel certain spell effects and counteracting Paradox, but even then they act like a catalyst that allows more supernal perfection to seep through the mage into this world, rather than being the sole source of those effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T04:40:05-07:00","id":1086549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1086250-essence-and-other-fuels?p=1086539#post1086539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Mana doesn't fuel spells, really. They can be used to fuel certain spell effects and counteracting Paradox, but even then they act like a catalyst that allows more supernal perfection to seep through the mage into this world, rather than being the sole source of those effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that &quot;catalyst&quot; is the right word, as catalysts aren't meant to be destroyed in the process of the reaction, while Mana is consumed by the spell. It is better represented as a kinetic control over the process (like, preforming the spell at &quot;higher temperature/pressure&quot;)- you rise the amount of energy in the system in order to change the mechanism in which you get the same product (spell effect) from the same reagents (the Mage).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T06:45:43-07:00","id":1086593,"title":"","content":"You're right, it's <b>a lot</b> more likely that Mages are kicking off some kind of metaphysical reaction than just making it out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> But my interpretation makes irresponsible mages even more scary than they already are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:39:53-07:00","id":1086627,"title":"","content":"Well, I wouldn't say it's not a fuel at all. You need mana to cast any non-Rote or non-Praxes spell that isn't one of your ruling Arcana. You might choose just to cast those spells, but that's always going to be more spells than you get freebies for, without universities' worth of Rotes. That implies that a strong connection to their Watchtower, or other Watchtowers through legacies or praxes or the pathways made by rotes, offers you sort of free fuel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-02-2017, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T10:24:18-07:00","id":1086692,"title":"","content":"Well, in a sense. Tinder is also fuel, but its role is to ignite the primary source of fuel, not being the sole source of heat. That's the way I've understood how mages tend to use Mana, even in non-ruling creative thaumaturgy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T10:31:54-07:00","id":1086700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1086250-essence-and-other-fuels?p=1086692#post1086692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in a sense. Tinder is also fuel, but its role is to ignite the primary source of fuel, not being the sole source of heat. That's the way I've understood how mages tend to use Mana, even in non-ruling creative thaumaturgy.</div> </div> </div> </div>So more of an accelerant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T11:03:03-07:00","id":1086714,"title":"","content":"That's the word. I'd claim language barrier, but I'm pretty sure it's the same word in Swedish too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The